Rename or copy this file to `KILL_SWITCH` (no extension) to halt the system.

While runtime/KILL_SWITCH exists:
  * no new positions are opened, in any mode
  * unfilled ENTRY orders are cancelled where it is safe to do so
  * protective exits (stops and reduce-only targets) are LEFT IN PLACE
  * existing positions are NOT force-closed

Closing positions is `flatten`, which needs FLATTEN_CONFIRMATION=CLOSE_ALL_POSITIONS.
That separation is deliberate: the kill switch is for "stop making it worse",
not "get me out at any price", and the two are different decisions.

The switch is checked before every entry decision and on every loop tick, so it
takes effect within one cycle. Deleting the file re-arms entries; nothing
resumes automatically while it is present.
